Allowed support is the first stated identity only; hide the remaining key while the learner completes it. Supported performance is practice, not an independent result.

## Rubric and independence

Required components: potential_outcomes_convex_weights_and_gap, pre_only_design_factor_fit_and_geometry, donor_context_feasibility_and_stability. Each full prompt/key below elicits every component; all are necessary for a pass on every permitted pair. Accept algebraically equivalent expressions and clearly defined opposite cash-flow signs with correct interpretation. A pass requires all requested outputs/reasons, correct units/assumptions and no critical conceptual error. Partial means a missing component or an unresolved isolated arithmetic slip with an otherwise valid method; independent correction is required for a pass. Fail means a critical mechanism/condition is wrong. Unscorable means a response or its help/exposure conditions cannot be established. Unknown help conditions are never independent evidence.

Critical errors: Negative weights called convex; post outcomes tune canonical design; perfect fit called proof of causal identification; contaminated donors ignored.

Acquisition requires two distinct unused unassisted full checks selected from the six exact metadata routes. Every I/D form covers all components; W1, S1, the prerequisite and C1 are forbidden substitutes. A D form used for acquisition cannot later be counted again as delayed success. No teach-generated item may replace a named full check; additional verified explanation/practice is allowed under the unchanged method and may not fabricate evidence. If fewer than two fresh forms remain for acquisition, return a plan_issue for an additional prepared bank.

| Component | I1 | I2 | D1 | D2 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| potential_outcomes_convex_weights_and_gap | required | required | required | required |
| pre_only_design_factor_fit_and_geometry | required | required | required | required |
| donor_context_feasibility_and_stability | required | required | required | required |

## Misconceptions and correction

An observed omitted term/sign is tentative until the learner explains it; compare the reasoning with the critical errors above. Score the original response before providing help. Route a conceptual failure to the relevant included derivation and prerequisite, then use an unused full form.

O010-C1, item_version 1, narrow_correction. **Prompt:** A researcher obtains a beautiful prefit by allowing large negative weights. Is that the same canonical estimator? **Key/rubric:** No. Nonnegative sum-one weights define canonical convex interpolation; unrestricted or shifted regression changes support and assumptions. Fit cannot replace contextual/stability checks. Pass requires all keyed reasoning; partial for a missing part; fail for the conflicting mechanism. This repairs a common inference only; it cannot substitute for a full numerical/capability check.

Give at most two hints (first identify the date/unit, second point to the included identity); after ineffective hints show the relevant worked step. After two unsuccessful independent attempts stop repeated quizzing, revisit the explanation/prerequisite and preserve the unresolved status.

## Immediate and delayed checks

### O010-I1

