**Complete solution and essential rubric:** $w_1=(5-3)/(5-1)=0.500000$ and $w_2=1-w_1=0.500000$; both are nonnegative and sum to one. The untreated prediction is $0.500000(8)+0.500000(12)=10.000000$ and estimated gap is $9-10.000000=-1.000000$. The observed treated potential outcome is available after intervention; its untreated potential outcome is missing. A target below the donor minimum cannot be exactly matched by a convex combination; negative/excess weights or an intercept can extrapolate but change the estimator. Canonical weights minimize $(X_1-X_0W)^\top V(X_1-X_0W)$ subject to nonnegative sum-one weights; nonnegative diagonal $V$ weights predictor mismatches as squared distances. Use pre-period data to fit/design; pre training/validation can choose $V$ then refit, without tuning to post gaps. The linear factor model separates common time effects, observed predictors, latent loadings/time-varying coefficients and transitory shocks. Matching predictors/pre outcomes can approximate latent loadings under the stated linear/stability/noise assumptions; more latent factors/noise and short prehistories can undermine it, and a huge donor pool can overfit. DID is a restricted time-invariant latent-coefficient case with relevant observed effects matched/controlled. Outside-hull/general-position projections can be unique with at most $k$ positive weights; inside-hull solutions may be nonunique, with a sparse solution using at most $k+1$. Neither sparsity nor fit proves identification. Donors must be untreated/uncontaminated and substantively comparable, with no anticipation or justified backdating, adequate history, stable post relation and credible overlap. Excluding spillover donors can impair fit; for negative donor spillovers the estimated negative treated effect can be attenuated. Long histories risk breaks, volatility reduces precision, demeaning requires a credible level shift, and nonlinear processes can defeat linear interpolation. The reported gap remains conditional on those checks, not a randomized comparison or universal SCM advantage. All requested calculations, derivations and qualifications are essential; the component map above applies to every full form.

I1/I2 are immediate checks; D1/D2 are distinct parallel variants reserved where possible for delayed checks. A delayed success requires an unused form before recap, no help/solution access, and at least 24 actual elapsed hours after acquisition and the most recent relevant teaching/solution exposure. Record intervening exposure. A calendar-date change alone is insufficient; an early D attempt is immediate evidence only.

